Your real gap is Research: unassessed, no evidence at all. For LSE Economics, that's a bigger liability than a third leadership title. It's also the exact reason your Execution/Project Depth and Intellectual Curiosity scores are only "developing" — you have activities, but no evidence of independent analytical work.

Concretely: the Youth Economics Research Fellowship (deadline Oct 1, 2026) fits this directly. It's economics-specific, matches your stated goal, and would be your first real research signal. With your 5–10 hr/week budget, that's a better use of time than founding another club you'd have to build from scratch.

